        <briefdescription>
<para>Parses <computeroutput>args</computeroutput> as <computeroutput>&lt;number&gt; &lt;operator&gt; &lt;number&gt;</computeroutput> and computes the result. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is the testable core of the application: it performs no I/O (it neither reads from <computeroutput>System.in</computeroutput> nor writes to <computeroutput>System.out</computeroutput>) and never blocks, so it can be called directly from tests and from scripts alike. Recognized operators are <computeroutput>+</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>-</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>*</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>/</computeroutput>. Invalid input (wrong argument count, non-numeric operand, unknown operator, division by zero) is reported as a descriptive <computeroutput>&quot;Error: ...&quot;</computeroutput> string instead of an uncaught exception, so the process always exits cleanly with a printable message.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>args</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The command-line arguments. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A human-readable result or error message. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
